cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SUCURI, please cite it as below."
title: "SUCURI: SymPy Unified Compiler for Unambiguous Rendered Input"
abstract: >-
  SUCURI reads LaTeX into SymPy without guessing: every ambiguity in the
  notation is either asked or settled by an explicit declaration. It covers
  index and index-free notation for differential geometry — connections,
  curvature, forms, proofs from stated hypotheses and component computations —
  with a notebook interface in English and Portuguese.
type: software
